WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.800
"The nation is fallen, yet mountains 
and rivers still exist.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.480
In spring, in the city, trees and grasses thrive."

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:12.940
Did Hideyoshi's dream of a united 
nation die along with him?

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.970
What does fate have in store?

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.490
A peaceful world at last?

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.530
Or even more warfare?

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:25.210
As Ieyasu's messenger, 
Nobuyuki visited Osaka Castle,

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:29.840
where he met Hideyori, the current Toyotomi 
clan head, for the first time.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.920
Meanwhile, having met Naomasa Ii

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.430
and fought Kotaro Fuma,

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:40.800
Yukimura regained his samurai warrior spirit.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.410
Halt, Yukimura Sanada!

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.170
Why, you...

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.770
Like my special chili bombs?

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.010
Guess not.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:53.950
<i>I shall uphold the vow of righteousness 
I shared with you, Lord Mitsunari.</i>

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.820
Edo Castle

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.100
I see.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.620
Then Naomasa is dead.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:02.870
Yes, sir.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:08.330
Until his dying breath, that man showed 
fealty to the Tokugawa clan.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.000
Indeed he did.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.250
Now that Yukimura's left Kudoyama, 
does that mean...

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:22.390
Yes.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:25.350
The die has been cast, if a bit earlier than expected.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:28.470
Are you saying that chaos will 
rear its ugly head once more?

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.020
That's right.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:34.360
That being the case, we must cleanse 
the pus while we still can.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.020
The pus?

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.530
Pardon the intrusion.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.550
What is it?

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.490
It's Lord Kato and Lord Fukushima...

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.450
My mind is made up.

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:56.990
I shall go to Osaka.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:04:01.510
And under Lord Hideyori, I'll return the 
Toyotomi clan to its rightful place.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:06.010
That's all very well, but will Lord 
Hideyori really forgive us?

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.500
We'll beg for his forgiveness!

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.520
We must bow our heads to the ground and 
apologize as many times as it takes!

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:14.770
Well, yeah.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.020
Right!

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.190
Let's go to Osaka!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.020
I was afraid of this.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.330
Osaka Castle

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:35.150
Inform Lord Ieyasu that I'll see him at Nijo Castle.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.320
What?

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.700
Lord Hideyori!

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:42.580
He desires to discuss future governance with me.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.830
How could I refuse?

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:46.240
Yes, sir.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:51.330
We should have a nice, long chat

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.050
about who will rule this country.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.840
<i>Hideyori Toyotomi...</i>

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:07.200
<i>What passes through his mind is a total mystery.</i>

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.090
If you don't want to die,

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.640
leave all your valuables and scram.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:30.760
<i>These men are no mere bandits.</i>

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.850
<i>Could it be?</i>

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.680
If I hand over everything I 
have, will you let me go?

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.600
Well, aren't you obedient?

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:46.010
Cut him!

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:46.990
Cut him down!

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:54.620
After him!

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:17.480
Sure is noisy around here...

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.670
Can't a man enjoy his nap in peace?

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.730
Who the hell are you?

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:29.200
I don't see why I should introduce myself 
to a bunch of pesky mosquitoes.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.490
Get in our way, and there will be dire consequences!

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:37.880
I'd say you're the ones who should 
be worried about consequences.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:41.750
If Hideyori catches wind of this, you're dead.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.670
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.500
Who's Lord Hideyori?

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:50.510
It's clear that you're vassals of the Toyotomi clan.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:55.260
If you're going to play bandits, you should 
at least pay attention to your swords.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:00.000
What kind of bandit carries a fine 
sword like that around?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:05.270
If word got out that Toyotomi samurai 
were acting like muggers,

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.200
it would ruin Hideyori's reputation.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:10.030
Q-Quiet!

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.770
Back down, and I'll pretend this never happened.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.030
Or would you rather...

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.420
...try to silence me?

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.670
Now, what will you do?

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.260
Damn you!

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:40.600
Go cool your head!

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.370
Who's next?

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.570
Run away!

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:52.860
He's a monster!

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:57.250
Thank you.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:59.580
Oh, no problem.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:04.080
You are Lord Keiji Maeda, yes?

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.140
How did you know?

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:09.310
Never mind. You could probably 
tell just by looking at me!

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:16.360
Keiji Maeda was the adopted nephew

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:18.050
Keiji Maeda

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.930
of Toshiie Maeda, Hideyoshi's trusted aide.

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:21.850
After deserting the Maeda clan,

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.100
he was living as a wandering samurai.

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.760
And you must be...

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:30.440
Six coins.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.300
Nobuyuki Sanada, correct?

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:40.610
Why did you agree to go to Nijo Castle?

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:48.420
You do realize that some of your men are just 
itching to fight the Tokugawa clan, right?

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:55.300
That doesn't mean I can declare war on them 
without hearing what they have to say first.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:59.250
They must be taught a lesson!

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.420
Now is the time for the Toyotomi 
clan to demonstrate their might!

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.960
Then, basically, you're saying...

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.060
You're prepared to go to war?

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:19.310
I dislike conflict.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:20.830
But...

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:24.330
If two powers lay claim to this country's rule,

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:27.640
that is bound to cause a few waves.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.830
And if they cannot stand side-by-side,

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.210
there can only be one.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.220
As I'm sure you've already heard,

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:48.020
Yukimura has escaped from 
his confines at Kudoyama.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:51.570
Also, Kiyomasa Kato and Masanori 
Fukushima have cut ties with us.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:54.860
It is likely they're headed to Osaka.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.010
Takatora Todo,

00:09:57.010 --> 00:10:00.730
I order you to eliminate Yukimura.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:03.120
Yes, sir.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.370
And Masamune Date,

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:08.910
I want you to track down and 
kill Kato and Fukushima.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:11.380
Yes, sir.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:15.560
Please wait.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:19.660
Could you leave Kato and Fukushima to me?

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.290
If I may,

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:24.390
I'd like to go after Yukimura.

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:28.030
You don't like our lord's orders?

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:29.520
That isn't it.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.890
It's only that Kato and Fukushima have a 
great history with the Toyotomi clan.

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:38.030
As someone with ties to the clan myself, 
I feel I should be the one to end them.

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:39.720
If I may be allowed,

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:46.790
I wish to be the one to kill the man who defeated 
Lord Hidetada's forces with a tiny army.

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:48.540
No.

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:49.480
But...

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:50.510
No!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.450
That is all.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:54.770
You may leave.

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:56.300
Yes, sir.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:02.070
Couldn't you have granted their requests?

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:05.450
As someone who served the Toyotomi clan myself,

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:09.310
I can understand why Takatora would want 
to take out Kiyomasa and Masanori.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:11.540
And as a samurai myself,

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:16.570
I can understand why Masamune would 
want to face the strongest foes.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:19.090
However,

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:24.550
in the days to come, samurai must be able 
to survive beyond the battlefield.

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:29.500
If we truly desire to put an end to warfare, 
and bring about a peaceful world,

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:33.330
we must rid ourselves of our fighting spirit.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:37.380
You want us to throw away the desire to fight?

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:38.560
Exactly.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:43.940
As such, I will not let them fight 
their desired opponents.

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:49.350
But what else is a samurai to do?

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.420
Administration.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:55.670
I wish us to take the skills to 
read the flow of battle,

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.610
devise strategy, and command troops,

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.990
and put them to good use toward 
this country's administration.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:08.120
Otherwise, there is no way we'll be able 
to maintain peace for centuries.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:12.220
Sounds difficult.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:15.660
Indeed.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:25.530
It's so tranquil, isn't it?

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.410
It is.

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:28.130
But...

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:34.680
Even rivers that seem to flow 
quietly have whirlpools within.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:36.390
Yes.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:39.860
Earlier, those were Toyotomi clan vassals.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:42.390
That they attacked me, a Tokugawa messenger,

00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:47.070
shows how much anti-Tokugawa 
sentiment exists within the clan.

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:49.350
Well, are you surprised?

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:54.730
Sure, the Tokugawa clan may have become Japan's 
rulers after the Battle of Sekigahara,

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:58.290
but it was Hideyoshi who unified 
the nation in the first place.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:01.850
If this keeps up, the Toyotomi clan will lose all face.

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.720
Lose face, huh?

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.680
Oh, yeah...

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:12.430
Have you heard

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.520
that your brother left Kudoyama?

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:22.530
I don't know the details, but they say 
all hell broke loose over there.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:26.510
<i>Yukimura left Kudoyama...</i>

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:31.190
In that case, he must be on 
his way to Osaka Castle.

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:32.920
I have to stop him!

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:34.040
Oh, come on...

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:36.790
Can't you sit still for a second?

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:40.290
That said, things are getting interesting.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:45.510
<i>Yukimura...</i>

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:51.490
Hey, Kiyomasa...

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:53.470
I know.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:56.680
Keep a close watch on our surroundings!

00:13:57.010 --> 00:13:57.830
Yes, sir.

00:13:58.300 --> 00:13:59.190
What's that?

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:07.450
They're here.

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:08.680
Take aim.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.200
Run!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:14.420
Open fire.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:17.860
Damn it!

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:20.120
They're trying to kill us before we reach Osaka!

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:43.270
Fools.

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:44.660
It was a trap.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:47.520
Please...

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:51.720
Let me join in the pursuit of Yukimura.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:52.870
I cannot.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:58.620
Since he's your brother, you might assist him.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.310
What are you saying?

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:00.960
I...

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:02.270
Quiet.

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.000
Detain this man.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:04.710
Yes, sir.

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:07.540
What are you doing, Takatora?

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:10.220
Nobuyuki, you'll stay here.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.520
We're regrouping with the scouts!

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.470
Yes, sir!

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:21.640
Damned Tokugawa lapdog!

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:23.250
Shut up!

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:25.650
You're just a fool who can't tell 
which way the wind blows!

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.070
This country belongs to the Toyotomi clan!

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:32.990
That's ancient history.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.720
It's so nice and cool.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.920
We're almost at Osaka.

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:47.920
Yes.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.600
Lord Takatora!

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.120
Yukimura Sanada!

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:05.740
Per Lord Ieyasu's orders,

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:08.270
I shall kill you!

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.410
Strike!

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:40.160
There's no end to them!

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:52.610
I'm here to lend you a hand, Yukimura Sanada!

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.730
That conspicuous outfit...

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:55.860
It can't be!

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.620
Lord Keiji Maeda?

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:00.950
You know who I am? That makes me happy!

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:02.750
Who called him?

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:12.340
I didn't want to be so rough.

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:14.010
Forgive me.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:17.260
But I must stop Yukimura right now.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.020
Don't let him escape!

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:51.790
After him!

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:55.800
Not on my watch.

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:02.680
What the...

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:14.690
<i>Yukimura!</i>

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.700
Thank you, Lord Keiji.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.540
No problem.

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:30.900
Brother...

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:33.680
Yukimura...

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:46.550
This is bad.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:54.480
Is this...

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:05.490
Lady Nene!

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.060
Now's our chance!

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:08.370
Follow us!

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:14.930
Curses...

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:22.820
We're really sorry!

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:23.890
What for?

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:30.630
We promised to work with Mitsunari 
and protect the Toyotomi clan,

00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:33.500
but we ended up fighting him at Sekigahara.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:34.650
Don't worry about it.

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:40.540
Both you two and Mitsunari did what 
you believed was right at the time.

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:42.530
So it's fine.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.400
Lady Nene...

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:50.370
Then, from now on, what do you two plan to do?

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:54.160
We shall head to Osaka and, under Lord Hideyori,

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:56.880
work ourselves to the bone for 
the sake of the Toyotomi clan.

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:59.350
Oh, is that so?

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:03.510
Take care of the Toyotomi clan, you hear me?

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:05.760
Lady Nene...

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.430
Why did you leave Kudoyama, Yukimura?

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:15.270
I have no excuse.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:17.080
But, Brother,

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:20.030
I did find the answer...

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:24.200
To the question you posed to me that day.

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.940
What it means for you to stay in this world.

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:30.040
Reconsider the meaning of your life.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:34.560
So long as I draw breath, I shall live for my beliefs.

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.040
I can live no other way.

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:40.720
You're going to Osaka, aren't you?

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:42.090
Yes.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:45.550
Is there no way we can serve the 
Tokugawa clan together?

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:48.730
Lord Mitsunari may be gone,

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:51.180
but the vow of righteousness 
I shared with him is not.

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:55.290
I have decided that the Toyotomi 
clan is where I belong.

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:57.740
Trying to stop you would be futile, I see...

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:02.710
You told me that you would protect 
the Sanada clan, as its pillar.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:06.000
In that case, I shall do my part and 
defend our pride as warriors...

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.220
Defend the soul of the Sanada!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.850
From here on,

00:21:21.010 --> 00:21:24.640
please don't consider me your little brother.

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:27.120
Very well.

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:30.720
The next time we meet in battle...

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:33.420
The next time...

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:36.570
I shall show no mercy!

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:36.570
I shall show no mercy!

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:38.870
Well, this is goodbye.

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:40.470
Farewell.

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:58.140
This parting of brothers would turn out

00:21:58.140 --> 00:22:01.630
to be the first step toward the war 
that would decide the fates

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:03.750
of the Toyotomi and Tokugawa clans.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>Episode 8</i>

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>The Path of No Return</i>

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
Sengoku Musou 
High School

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
8th Period

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:48.400
Japan's finest sweet bean bread, here I come!

00:23:48.650 --> 00:23:50.400
School Store

